# Paths graphify leaves out of the knowledge graph (gitignore syntax; .gitignore
# is applied too). Ported test262/TypeScript suites are test data, not source, and
# would otherwise dominate the graph with thousands of disconnected fixture nodes.
# Everything else under crates/conformance/ stays in. The interpreter's own
# tests/fixtures/ also stay: they are the required demonstration of each language
# feature, and agents look up which fixture covers a behavior.
crates/conformance/cases/
crates/conformance/rejected/
# Exclude the suite's contents rather than the directory so its README stays in;
# a negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
crates/conformance/typescript/*
!crates/conformance/typescript/README.md
